From a0670bdb83bb5fe8994d2e1e0d4fde9f6565e2fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:13:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Prose Display (S2): live resize agent, mode-hint wait, REDRAW

prose_display driver: PRDS_WAIT_MODE_HINT ioctl blocks (with timeout,
interruptible) until the host sends a MODE_HINT and returns the host's
preferred size; the semaphore behind it stays kernel-owned because the
wait happens inside the ioctl. REDRAW events bump redraw_count in the
shared info. The retrace semaphore is only handed over while the kernel
still owns it, so clones and the agent don't steal it from app_server.

prose_display.accelerant: a changed redraw_count makes the commit thread
send a full-surface commit.

prose_display_agent (new server, launched from data/launch/system):
waits for mode hints and switches the screen with BScreen::SetMode()
(timing from compute_display_timing, any size up to the maximum), so the
guest desktop follows the host window like guest tools do on other
hypervisors. Without the device it idles.

Verified on VZ: hvgpu --resize-after 45 1600x1000 -> MODE_HINT 1600x935
-> agent: "1280x800 -> 1600x935: No error" -> SET_MODE 1600x935 stride
6400 on the host within 160 ms; the desktop re-rendered at the new size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
